<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Cemig cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Cemig cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings said it had reduced its rating for Brazilian utility Companhia Energetica de Minas Gerais, or Cemig, to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Charles Barnett wrote in a Feb 25 report that he had reduced the rating on the basis of price.</p>
<p>-- The shares &quot;have been a start performer over the past four months.  They have risen 43 percent and have outperformed the Bovespa index by nearly five percent,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Shares in the power company were off 1.40 reais to 46 in Sao Paulo.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
